# L §5.11 Logic: "`if c then a else b` evaluates only the branch c takes; with a hole c it evaluates both, and
# is a hole unless they are equal."  L §8.1: a hole stops propagating at "an `if` whose branches are equal".
# h has no row (a hole); m = 0, so both branches are 0 (the bare 0 takes the type of the whole, L §3.2 Inline
# figures): z = 0, and the hole is not printed.  (Found by the lead: the core printed ?"Is it?".)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2027-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2027-12-31

source s "s"
input h: bool question "Is it?"
input m: num
def z: num = if h then 0 else m at reader

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  m = 0

ask qz: z law 2026-12-31
=== expect
qz: 0
  law date 2026-12-31, cut 2027-01-01
